Z||000000||count_iblis||10-30-2000||06:53 AM||||Does anyone else have trouble trying to get full coverage insurance on thier Fiero?  I have a friend that has it on his, but the two insuracne companys I go through wont do it. They said that they dont insure full coverage on cars 15 years or older?  Its an 1985 gt?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Predator||10-30-2000||07:21 AM||||I checked into full coverage on my 1985 GT, and they would insure it (AllState). The only problem is they only give you blue book value on the car not what it is worth, and not replacement value. If you want that you have to get classic car insurance which is out the ying yang. I decided to go with no fault. The premiems were so much higher for full coverage that it wasn't worth what they would give me if the car was wrecked. This is just my opinion. Others may have had better luck. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-30-2000||07:36 AM||||You may want to check into a specified $ ammount. Photos and qualified apprasial may both be required.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-30-2000||09:04 AM||||My car is insured by Nationwide. I have it insured as a "Collectable" (appraisal required) Total annual cost is $119. (It is stored during the winter so it's $110 every 6 months and $9.00 while it is stored) But I used to have it as a daily driver and insurance was $265 a year. Most insurance companies will insure it for full coverage if you have an appraisal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||286SE'S||10-30-2000||03:26 PM||||My VW is a 71, I have no problem with getting full coverage. I only have it because they are so easy to steal.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||10-30-2000||03:48 PM||||I have AllState Full Covrage on my 85 coupe. I told him it was a Show Car. I pay $59.00 a year. <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif"> <BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A>-                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||2
Z||000006||DavidHenshaw||10-31-2000||07:29 PM||||Haze, you may have trouble collecting at claim time if the car is not actually a "show" car. I'm not a claim adjuster but I am an insurance agent. <P>My guess is the adjuster of your claim would want to know what shows you had participated in during the past year. Also, which show you were participating in when you claim occured and would also ask for documentation of your car having been showed at different events.<P>Adjusters have so much experience with slight of hand by insureds they get to be mind readers. If the wording of your policy endorsement makes any mention of the coverage being special use you probably don't have any coverage.<P>Dave<P>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
